<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#gauleiter">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gauleiter</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A Gauleiter was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazi Party</a>'s leader of a regional branch, or Gau, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and later in annexed territories. Appointed by Hitler and answerable to him alone, Gauleiters often also held state offices such as Reich governor, and during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, as Reich defence commissioners, they gained wide powers over civil defence, labour and evacuation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gauleiter.jpg" alt="Gauleiter" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tractor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gauleiter.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
